1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,920
This Dispatch workflow handles the
whole customer order in one delivery.

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:10,160
We will print the pick and packing lists,
complete each operation for the full

3
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:11,900
order, and confirm shipment.

4
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:17,123
Step one: Review the Confirmed order.

5
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:23,343
Find the customer order and check its delivery
address, quantities, and availability of the

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:25,063
physical goods before starting.

7
00:00:27,583 --> 00:00:29,723
Step two: Print the Pick List.

8
00:00:30,383 --> 00:00:36,323
Select the order, open Export, choose
its pick template, and generate the PDF.

9
00:00:36,983 --> 00:00:42,943
Administrators can customize template names;
this example uses Warehouse collection sheet.

10
00:00:45,542 --> 00:00:48,642
Use the paper list to collect all four pieces.

11
00:00:49,362 --> 00:00:53,262
Check the article and physical source shelf, then tick Done.

12
00:00:53,782 --> 00:00:55,762
Printing does not mark anything picked.

13
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:01,117
Step three: Mark the whole order Picked.

14
00:01:01,797 --> 00:01:03,117
Choose Mark Picked from Actions.

15
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:08,257
In this customized workspace the
button is called Collect entire order.

16
00:01:08,877 --> 00:01:11,617
Confirm only after collecting every line.

17
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:15,527
Check the completion result.

18
00:01:16,107 --> 00:01:19,407
The line is fully picked and packing has not started.

19
00:01:19,887 --> 00:01:22,767
This records progress; it does not confirm shipment.

20
00:01:25,542 --> 00:01:27,842
Step four: Print the Packing List.

21
00:01:28,702 --> 00:01:31,742
Return to Export and choose the packing template.

22
00:01:32,442 --> 00:01:36,222
Check the delivery address and
contents against the complete order.

23
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:43,775
Pack all four pieces and tick the paper
checklist after checking the contents.

24
00:01:44,535 --> 00:01:49,495
The list describes the whole order rather
than individual parcel allocations.

25
00:01:52,417 --> 00:01:55,157
Step five: Mark the whole order Packed.

26
00:01:55,597 --> 00:01:58,837
Choose Mark Packed and confirm after all goods are packed.

27
00:01:59,477 --> 00:02:01,857
Every line must already be fully picked.

28
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,880
Verify that picking and packing are complete.

29
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:11,800
The Sales Order remains Confirmed until you record dispatch.

30
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:16,260
Repeating a completed action does not add more quantity.

31
00:02:18,917 --> 00:02:21,397
Step six: Confirm the full shipment.

32
00:02:22,077 --> 00:02:27,077
When the complete order is actually being
dispatched, choose Change State, select Shipped,

33
00:02:27,297 --> 00:02:27,637
and apply.

34
00:02:30,375 --> 00:02:31,835
Check the transition result.

35
00:02:32,455 --> 00:02:35,595
This example records a successful full shipment.

36
00:02:36,495 --> 00:02:41,095
Physical stock deduction also depends on the
article being configured as a stock item;

37
00:02:41,575 --> 00:02:44,635
picking and packing alone never deduct stock.

38
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:52,132
Reopen the order lines and verify
that the delivered line is Complete.

39
00:02:52,772 --> 00:02:55,072
The full-order Dispatch workflow is finished.

40
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:00,453
Pause for details and follow the full guide.
